comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T09:04:26.135Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence (branch feat/extension-authoring-contracts, 2026-11-07).\n\nProbe of the built 2026.11.7 CLI against a sandbox extension (pm demo-brief with --item-id, --status-filter, --commit), one host flag per run:\n- accepted: --json, --lean, --token-accounting, --output-format, --quiet, --no-changed-fields, --full-changed-fields, --id-only, --pm-path (alias --path), --no-pager, --profile, --help, --author, --expect-hash (refuses a malformed revision, accepts id=item_hash);\n- refused on a non-read command: --output-include, --output-limit, --output-budget, --output-session, --output-cursor, --output-row-contract (Universal output controls apply only to read commands);\n- --no-extensions removes the command itself (unknown command);\n- root-only --all and --explain leaked into the handler options as all/explain = true.\n\nChange:\n- RESERVED_EXTENSION_HOST_FLAGS declares extension_command_availability per flag (read_output for the six read-output controls, never for --no-extensions) and discovery_value_name path for --pm-path, so availability is data next to the reservation.\n- resolveExtensionCommandInheritedFlagContracts derives the applicable host rows (owner host, reservation_scope inherited, value_arity, value_name).\n- pm contracts --command <ext> --flags-only --json gains inherited_flags for registered extension commands (help and item, which are core commands without a core flag table, are excluded); every extension row carries owner extension and sdk_option.\n- pm help <ext> --json gains inherited_options (same rows, owner host); options rows carry owner and sdk_option. Text help prints an Inherited host flags section that points at the contracts command.\n- CLI dispatch refuses an undeclared root-only flag on an extension command with the existing unknown-option refusal instead of leaking it.\n\nVerified by tests/integration/extensions/extension-option-contract.integration.spec.ts: it reads inherited_flags from the contract, invokes every listed flag (except --help) on a mutating command that records a comment, and expects exit 0 for each; it asserts --json, --author, --pm-path, --output-format and --expect-hash are listed (negative control: dropping the rows fails), that excluded flags stay out, that text and JSON help carry the same set, and that --all/--explain are refused.\n\nFollow-ups filed: pm-4of199 (a command that declares NO flags still hands any undeclared option to its handler; the unknown-option message lists flags the command refuses) and pm-6vk110 (core per-command contracts and help omit inherited host flags too).\n"
  "2026-11-07T10:00:02.980Z","harness:claude-code","Codex round 1 on the batch: the undeclared root-only refusal (--all/--explain) now runs in the extension action wrapper for every extension command, including commands that declare no flags; covered by the integration spec with demo-plain. Details on pm-gh1665."
  "2026-11-07T13:29:07.990Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review on PR 1682: an extension could register --output_limit (an underscore spelling the CLI folds into the reserved --output-limit) because the reserved-name check compared the exact spelling. validateExtensionLongFlagToken now also checks the kebab form, so underscore spellings of host flags are refused as host_owned_flag_collision; regression in tests/unit/core/extension-flag-definition-validation.spec.ts."
